# <project-or-workspace-name> context instructions

## Use the Context Mode index first

This `<project-or-workspace-kind>` contains `<repository-scope>`. Its Context
Mode project index uses the source label `<project-or-workspace-name> context`
and is refreshed by `.github/hooks/reindex-workspace.json` on Claude Code
`sessionStart`. After a successful run, the hook reports the indexed file and
section counts in the Claude Code session. In the first response, explicitly
confirm the ready status using those exact counts. If no ready status is
available or the hook reports a failure, do not claim that the index is fresh.

Start Claude Code from `<project-or-workspace-root>`. Before using `grep`, `rg`,
`find`, or broad manual directory listings to understand the codebase, search
the existing index:

```text
ctx_search(
  queries: ["your focused question"],
  source: "<project-or-workspace-name> context"
)
```

Use `ctx_execute` or `ctx_execute_file` to count, filter, compare, or summarize
indexed content without loading raw repository output into the conversation.
For exact edits, read the target file directly after locating it through the
index.

The index includes `<indexed-content-scope>`. It excludes
`<excluded-content-scope>`.
